BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fourth Annual World Music &amp\; Dance Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T210000
UID:691bdfe9127354636be7115d@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore and enjoy music and dance from around the world!\nCele
 brate the rhythms\, cultures\, and global creativity that make our communi
 ty shine at the\nOccidental World Music & Dance Festival\n! This joyful\, 
 immersive event brings together extraordinary musicians and dancers from a
 round the world for a day filled with exhilarating performances\, interact
 ive workshops\, and irresistible rhythms. From captivating traditional art
 istry to innovative contemporary fusion\, the festival invites audiences o
 f all ages to experience the beauty of global cultures up close. With food
 \, vendors\, community activities\, and plenty of space to dance\, it’s 
 a feast for the senses and a celebration of unity through music and moveme
 nt. Come be part of one of Occidental’s most beloved and uplifting tradi
 tions!\nMore Than 40 sessions to choose from!\nEnjoy a variety of performa
 nces\, workshops\, jams\, drum circles and demonstrations\nplus:\nMusical 
 Instrument Lending Library\nCeltic Harp Encounter\nArt Gallery\nFree instr
 ument check • Free parking\nLata’s Indian Cuisine\nGet tickets\nTicket
  prices - adults\n$65 through April 30\n$75 through May 29\n$80 at the doo
 r\nKids 12 and under free\nTeens half price\, Discounts for OCA members.\n
 Get your tickets early and save!\nA limited number of scholarships is avai
 lable.\nClick here to apply for a scholarship to the event.\nScroll down t
 o see the list of presenters.\nSponsored by:\nLoveland Violin Shop\nLiving
  History Centre\nInterested in sponsorship? Please contact us!\nDodona\nPE
 RFORMANCES\nNative American Pomo Dancers\nSol Flamenco\nJenny Kerr & Frien
 ds - Southern Delta Blues\nKhatch Khatchadourian - Armenian Music\nStory W
 rens\nWill Marsh - Sitar music of India\nJoss Jaffe - Tabla\, West African
  N’goni\nDodona - Music of Epirus & Albania\nLos Bahianatos\nGradina - B
 alkan Music\nMeredith Axelrod and Craig Ventresco - Ragtime\nCarey Dubbert
  and Meredith Axelrod - Autoharp\nGradina\nKatiana Vilá - Iberian Songs\n
 Los Bahianatos - Colombian Cumbia & Vallenato\nMichael Hubbert - Uilleann 
 Bagpipes\nKhatch Khatchadourian\nRaman Osman - Kurdish Music\nJanessa Lynn
 a - Belly Dance\nStory Wrens - Story Songs of the British Isles\nBobby Edw
 ards - Swiss Alpenhorn\nKen Genetti - Zithers from Around the World\nScrol
